h evidence.\n\nFEEDBACK\nDiwali and Christmas are religious celebrations for many people and also cultural. The show is local community. Harmony Day celebrates cultural diversity.","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect claim as a comparison. Name its specific HSIE error, then show the corrected evidence-based claim.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner base claims on sources, places and respectful community knowledge, rather than guessing from a single picture. Keep every claim linked to evidence.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the sources, map features or community examples that carry the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your record with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your evidence? If a detail is uncertain, identify what source you would need next. One deliberate, evidence-based revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Changing the wording without repairing the evidence does not fix the error. Believing everyone in a country celebrates the same things ignores the many cultures within a community. Correct the claim or use of sources, not just the neatness of the poster.","title":"Test a misconception"},{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Use the same HSIE idea on a new place, person, source or context, not a copy of the worked example.","options":["A guess with no evidence","A claim unrelated to the source or place","Use the same HSIE idea on a new place, person, source or context, not a copy of the worked example","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about celebration with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nCommunities celebrate for many reasons, such as culture, religion, harvest, history or friendship. Examples include Lunar New Year, Diwali, Eid, Christmas, Harmony Day and local shows. Celebrations help people sh